{% extends 'partials/base.html.twig' %}
{% set hero_image_name = page.header.hero_image %}

{% block hero %}
    {% if hero_image_name %}
        {% set hero_image = page.media[hero_image_name] %}
        {% set content %}
            <h1>{{ page.title }}</h1>
            {% if page.header.subtitle %}<p class="lead">{{ page.header.subtitle }}</p>{% endif %}
        {% endset %}
        {% include 'partials/hero.html.twig' with {id: 'blog-hero'} %}
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    <article class="content-item">
        {{ page.content|raw }}
        <h2>AJAX</h2>
        <p>The core of htmx is a set of attributes that allow you to issue AJAX requests directly from HTML:</p>
        
        <h3>hx-put</h3>
        <pre><code>
&lt;button hx-put="/home/messages"&gt;
    Put To Messages
&lt;/button&gt;
</code></pre>
        <p>This tells the browser:<br>
            When a user clicks on this button, issue a PUT request to the URL /home/_messages and load the response into the button</p>
        
        {# Pour le module messages #}
        {% for module in page.collection() if module.slug == '_messages' %}
            {{ module.content|raw }}
        {% endfor %}

        <hr/>
        
        <h3>hx-post</h3>
        <p> Here is a <code>div</code> that posts to <code>/home/mouse_entered</code> when a mouse enters it:</p>
        <pre><code>&lt;div hx-post="/home/_mouse_entered" hx-trigger="mouseenter"&gt;
    [Here Mouse, Mouse!]
&lt;div&gt;</code></pre>
        
        {# CORRECTION : On cherche le module 'mouse_entered' #}
        {% for module in page.collection() if module.slug == '_mouse_entered' %}
            {{ module.content|raw }}
        {% endfor %}
        
        <h3>hx-get</h3>
        <p>You can use these attributes to implement many common UX patterns, such as Active Search</p>
        <pre>
            <code>
  &lt;input type="text" name="q"
    hx-get="/home/_trigger_delay"
    hx-trigger="keyup changed delay:500ms"
    hx-target="#search-results"
    placeholder="Search..."&gt;
&lt;div id="search-results"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
</code>
        </pre>
        <p>This input will issue a request 500 milliseconds after a key up event if the input has been changed and inserts the results into the div with the id <code>search-results</code>.</p>
        
        {% for module in page.collection() if module.slug == '_messages' %}
            {% include 'modular/messages.html.twig' with {page: module} %}
        {% endfor %}

        
        <h3>hx-patch</h3>
        <p>The hx-patch attribute will cause an element to issue a PATCH to the specified URL and swap the HTML into the DOM using a swap strategy:</p>
        <pre><code>&lt;button hx-patch="/home/_patch" hx-target="body"&gt;
  Patch Your Account
&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>
        <p>This example will cause the button to issue a PATCH to /_patch and swap the returned HTML into the innerHTML of the body.</p>
        
        <h3>hx-delete</h3>
        <p>The hx-delete attribute will cause an element to issue a DELETE to the specified URL and swap the HTML into the DOM using a swap strategy:</p>
        <pre>
            <code>
        &lt;button hx-delete="/home/_delete" hx-target="body"&gt;
        Delete Your Account
        &lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>
        <p>This example will cause the button to issue a DELETE to /_delete and swap the returned HTML into the innerHTML of the body.</p>
        
        {# CORRECTION : On cherche le module 'account' #}
        {% for module in page.collection() if module.slug == '_account' %}
            {{ module.content|raw }}
        {% endfor %}

    </article>
{% endblock %}
